## Initial design hypotheses

1. A single event-loop owner of all writes can provide a legal cancellation/
   terminal ordering at the native write boundary, while four worker threads
   provide encoding concurrency. Implemented; protocol, concurrent-client,
   crash, and recovery tests support this design. Deterministic interposed
   barrier qualification remains external, unexecuted evidence.
2. Nonblocking sockets and bounded queues can isolate slow/disconnected clients
   from encoding ownership and durable transitions. Implemented; disconnect and
   pipelining tests pass. Review found and fixed rescanning of growing input
   lines and retention of already-sent output prefixes.

These are initial correctness/design hypotheses. No optimization-round
hypothesis, group commit, kernel replacement, or durability relaxation was
attempted. No benchmark conclusions are drawn from test elapsed times.

## Attempts, including failures

| Attempt | Outcome and action |
|---|---|
| Initial ReleaseSafe build | Failed translating glibc fortified `fcntl` wrappers. Set `_FORTIFY_SOURCE=0` in the host C import and explicitly enabled GNU declarations. This affects imported libc header wrappers, not the unchanged kernel or storage durability. |
| Next build | Failed because GNU `bind` uses a translated transparent socket-address union. Passed the union's Unix-address member explicitly; handled `accept4` likewise. |
| Next build | Failed because Zig 0.16 JSON object-map `put` requires an allocator. Supplied the request arena allocator. |
| First successful build | Public smoke passed. |
| First eight-test run | Seven passed; crash-history test timed out while its client sent many small pipeline messages without reading responses. This was a test-client flow-control failure. Changed that crash burst to one buffered send; retained the failed run in broker responses. |
| Second eight-test run | All eight passed, including process-crash restart and cancellation-intent preservation. |
| Expanded 13-test run | Passed, including 40 MiB text, 16 MiB aggregate input, 64 MiB outstanding payload, fragmented transport, and malformed recovery records. |
| Expanded 15-test run | Passed, adding 1,024-job backpressure and drain semantics. Known-ID retries were kept idempotent during drain. |
| Fresh-counter correction | Added the explicit fresh-database exception for absent zero counters, retaining rejection for missing counters in a nonempty database. |
| ReleaseSafe and Debug, 16 tests | Both passed, plus public smoke. Logs: `tmp/release-validation.log`, `tmp/debug-validation.log`. |
| Native boundary fixture test | Passed for nonempty legacy/witness fixtures, relative prefix consumption, distinct witness digest, 4,096-item success, and 4,097-item resource failure. Log: `tmp/native-boundary-validation.log`. |
| Final output-buffer review | Added sent-prefix compaction to bound memory during continuous event output. Final release/debug validation follows this change. |
| Final ReleaseSafe and Debug validation | Public smoke plus all 17 tests passed in both builds. Suite times were 4.996 s and 8.543 s, respectively; these are test timings, not performance trial results. Logs: `tmp/final-release-validation.log`, `tmp/final-debug-validation.log`. |

## Infrastructure and diagnostic observations

